# Only read when EXPO_PUBLIC_DATA_ADAPTER=supabase (src/data/composition-root.tsx).
# The memory adapter — the default, and what every existing typecheck/lint/
# jest/web:export step runs against — needs none of this.
#
# M7 is a scaffold: the schema, RLS and adapter code under supabase/ and
# src/data/adapters/supabase/ are real and reviewable, but have never been
# run against an actual Supabase project. Provisioning one, running
# `supabase db push` (or applying supabase/migrations/*.sql in order) against
# it, and filling these in is what turns the scaffold on.
EXPO_PUBLIC_DATA_ADAPTER=memory

# Project Settings -> API in the Supabase dashboard.
EXPO_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=
EXPO_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=

# Google OAuth needs no env var here — auth.ts's signInWithGoogle uses
# expo-auth-session's makeRedirectUri(), which reads app.json's own
# "scheme" (already "youdo"). What it does need, entirely on the
# Supabase/Google side, not in this file: Authentication -> Providers ->
# Google enabled in the Supabase dashboard, a matching OAuth client in
# Google Cloud Console, and that client's redirect URI registered as
# <scheme>://Project Settings -> API's own auth callback path — see
# Supabase's Expo/React Native auth guide for the exact value.
